<Prefab>
  <!-- Narrative stage screen - the shared shell behind Family/Early Childhood/Adolescence/Youth/Young
       Adulthood/Starting Age (all six use this exact same movie/prefab natively, only the VM's Title/
       Description/SelectionList content differs per stage, driven by TAOM's own ModuleData\charactercreation\
       *_menu.json files - untouched by this file).
       LAYOUT PASS 4 (2026-09-26, user feedback on LAYOUT PASS 2/3 below): "the right panel just dont look
       good... make the left panel also on the right like in my image" - BOTH panels now live on the right
       side (ledger further from the edge, options panel flush right), leaving the ENTIRE left+center area
       open for the character scene. This also naturally addresses the camera-centering complaint from PASS 3
       (the camera itself is still native/unmovable - see LeftPanel's own comment - but a much wider open
       canvas on the left makes wherever the fixed camera puts the characters read as comfortably framed,
       without needing LAYOUT PASS 3's panel-width distortion hack, which is REVERTED this pass: both panels
       are back to their own undistorted native sizes). A deliberate gap between the two right-side panels
       holds the Next button, so it stays clear of both without needing a huge screen-spanning margin.
       Z-ORDER FIX (same feedback): "both panels need to be beneath the top ribbon, the blending art needs to
       be above top ribbon and panels" - PASS 2/3 had the ribbon declared BEFORE the panels, so a panel's own
       top edge (LeftPanel was full screen height) drew OVER the ribbon wherever they overlapped. Reordered to
       match FaceGen's own proven convention exactly: panels first, ribbon after (draws on top of panels),
       corner ornament last (draws on top of both).
       CHROME PASS (2026-09-26): this screen reuses TAOMFaceGen.xml's ribbon/corner-ornament chrome. The
       ribbon's three entries are a real stage-jump breadcrumb (FACTION/CHARACTER jump to earlier character-
       creation stages via StageJumpButton.cs; ORIGINS is this screen, inert) rather than FaceGen's own
       tab-switching, since this screen has no tabs of its own.
       Root widget type, PreviousButton/NextButton paths, and every @-binding/{DataSource} name below are
       preserved byte-for-byte from the native prefab (Modules\Native\GUI\Prefabs\CharacterCreation\
       CharacterCreationNarrativeStage.xml) - only the visual layer + ItemList's nesting path changed. See
       C:\Users\Niels\.claude\plans\starry-tickling-seahorse.md for the full reasoning/research trail. -->
  <Window>
    <CharacterCreationNarrativeStageScreenWidget DoNotAcceptEvents="true" WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" PreviousButton="PrevButton" NextButton="NextButton" ItemList="OptionsPanel\OptionsInnerPanel\OptionsScrollablePanel\OptionsClipRect\OptionsList\ItemList">
      <Children>

        <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" SuggestedWidth="746" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Sprite="fs_scrim_l" AlphaFactor="0.85" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
        <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" SuggestedWidth="746" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Sprite="fs_scrim_r" AlphaFactor="0.85" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />

        <!-- Traits gained this stage (e.g. Mercy/Valor). Same card-frame fix as the skill icons above -
             EncyclopediaHeroTraitVisualWidget also just sets its own Sprite directly in native code
             (SPGeneral\SPTraits\<id>_<value>, confirmed via decompile), no frame of its own. -->
        <ListPanel DataSource="{GainedPropertiesController\GainedTraits}" WidthSizePolicy="CoverChildren" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" HorizontalAlignment="Right" MarginRight="594" MarginTop="110" StackLayout.LayoutMethod="HorizontalRightToLeft" DoNotUseCustomScaleAndChildren="true">
          <ItemTemplate>
            <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="82" SuggestedHeight="83" MarginLeft="6">
              <Children>
                <Widget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" Sprite="cc_card_9" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
                <EncyclopediaHeroTraitVisualWidget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="74" SuggestedHeight="75" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" TraitId="@TraitId" TraitValue="@Value">
                  <Children>
                    <HintWidget DataSource="{Hint}" WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" Command.HoverBegin="ExecuteBeginHint" Command.HoverEnd="ExecuteEndHint" />
                  </Children>
                </EncyclopediaHeroTraitVisualWidget>
              </Children>
            </Widget>
          </ItemTemplate>
        </ListPanel>

        <!-- Ledger panel (skill/attribute list) - LAYOUT PASS 6 (2026-09-26, user report: "the left panel
             isnt on the left side of the screen, move it left its overlapping the viewport"): LAYOUT PASS 4
             positioned this via HorizontalAlignment="Right" + a computed MarginRight so it sat immediately
             left of OptionsPanel - which left a dead gap between it and the TRUE screen edge while its own
             right edge intruded further into the viewport than intended. Back to true flush-left
             (HorizontalAlignment="Left", no margin) - the ledger sits at the real left edge, OptionsPanel
             at the real right edge, character in the genuinely open middle. Native undistorted size (546x1080,
             matching FaceGen's own cc_panel_bg usage exactly). -->
        <Widget Id="LeftPanel" WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="546" SuggestedHeight="1080" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Sprite="cc_panel_bg" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" DoNotUseCustomScaleAndChildren="true">
          <Children>

            <FrontEndTextWidget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="400" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedHeight="44" HorizontalAlignment="Center" MarginTop="98" Brush="CC.Title" LocalizedText="{=taom_fui_skills_and_attributes}Skills &amp; Attributes" />
            <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="310" SuggestedHeight="16" HorizontalAlignment="Center" MarginTop="152" Sprite="fs_divider_wide" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />

            <!-- No scroll here (user report: "the left panel with skills has a scrollbar, its not needed the
                 entirety fits without having to scroll") - the ledger's real content (6 base-attribute groups
                 + OtherSkills) is a fixed structure that comfortably fits this space with room to spare,
                 confirmed from an in-game screenshot. Plain CoverChildren wrapper instead of ScrollablePanel/
                 ClipRect/List/Scrollbar, same simplification already applied to TFGGrid.xml earlier this
                 project when scroll turned out unnecessary there too. -->
            <Widget Id="InnerPanel" WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="460" SuggestedHeight="760" MarginTop="195" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top">
              <Children>

                <TAOMGainedProperties DataSource="{GainedPropertiesController}" Sprite="" MarginTop="0" MarginLeft="0" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top" AlphaFactor="1" />

              </Children>
            </Widget>

          </Children>
        </Widget>

        <!-- The life-stage choice panel - LAYOUT PASS 5 (2026-09-26, user feedback on LAYOUT PASS 4: "match
             both panels' visual style"): now uses the SAME cc_panel_bg sprite/546x1080 size/Title+divider
             treatment as LeftPanel above, instead of the previous round's custom chamfered/tabbed
             cc_options_panel.png shape - the two panels read as a matching pair now, per the user's own
             mirrored reference image showing the same panel look on both sides. cc_options_panel.png itself
             is left in Sprites (unused) in case the tab-shaped look is ever wanted back for something else.
             Static "Skills & Attributes" title mirrors as a dynamic "@Title" here (the stage name, e.g.
             "Family") - same position/brush as LeftPanel's own title, giving this panel a proper header too
             instead of relying solely on the in-content @Description/@SelectionText text. Structurally
             identical content below the title to previous rounds (Description/SelectionText/option list/
             selected-option summary all in one scrollable card) - only the outer shell has changed across
             rounds, not what's inside it.
             FLIPPED (2026-09-26, user request: "can you flip the image of the panel horizontally?"): uses
             cc_panel_bg_r.png, a horizontally-mirrored copy of cc_panel_bg.png (System.Drawing RotateFlipType.
             FlipX), so the two panels read as mirror images of each other (like two facing pages) rather than
             identical copies - purely cosmetic, no layout/size change. -->
        <Widget Id="OptionsPanel" WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="546" SuggestedHeight="1080" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Sprite="cc_panel_bg_r" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" DoNotUseCustomScaleAndChildren="true">
          <Children>

            <TextWidget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="400" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedHeight="44" HorizontalAlignment="Center" MarginTop="98" Brush="CC.Title" Text="@Title" />
            <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="310" SuggestedHeight="16" HorizontalAlignment="Center" MarginTop="152" Sprite="fs_divider_wide" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />

            <Widget Id="OptionsInnerPanel" WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="460" SuggestedHeight="760" MarginTop="195" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top">
              <Children>

                <ScrollablePanel Id="OptionsScrollablePanel" WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" AutoHideScrollBars="true" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" ClipRect="OptionsClipRect" InnerPanel="OptionsClipRect\OptionsList" VerticalScrollbar="..\OptionsVerticalScrollbar">
                  <Children>

                    <Widget Id="OptionsClipRect" WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" ClipContents="true">
                      <Children>

                        <ListPanel Id="OptionsList" WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top" StackLayout.LayoutMethod="VerticalTopToBottom">
                          <Children>

                            <!-- Stage flavor text, always shown. -->
                            <TextWidget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" MarginRight="16" MarginBottom="16" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top" Brush="CC.NarrativeBody" Text="@Description" ClipContents="false" />

                            <!-- "Choose one..." prompt, hidden once an option is picked. -->
                            <TextWidget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" MarginBottom="12" Brush="CC.NarrativeOption" IsHidden="@AnyItemSelected" Text="@SelectionText" />

                            <NavigationScopeTargeter ScopeID="ItemsScope" ScopeParent="..\ItemList" ScopeMovements="Vertical" HasCircularMovement="true" IsDefaultNavigationScope="true" />
                            <NavigatableListPanel Id="ItemList" DataSource="{SelectionList}" WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" MarginBottom="16" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" StackLayout.LayoutMethod="VerticalTopToBottom" MinIndex="0" MaxIndex="1000" ParentPanel="..\..\..\..\OptionsScrollablePanel" AutoScrollTopOffset="70" AutoScrollBottomOffset="70">
                              <ItemTemplate>
                                <!-- frameless option row: near-invisible wash at rest, gold accent bar + bright
                                     text once selected/hovered - see CC.NarrativeOption*/CC.NarrativeOptionRow
                                     in Brushes\CharCreation.xml. Accent bar is Fixed height (matching MinHeight)
                                     rather than StretchToParent, avoiding the project's documented
                                     StretchToParent-inside-CoverChildren ballooning bug. -->
                                <ButtonWidget DoNotPassEventsToChildren="true" WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" MinHeight="90" MarginBottom="6" Brush="CC.NarrativeOptionRow" Command.Click="ExecuteSelect" IsSelected="@IsSelected" UpdateChildrenStates="true">
                                  <Children>
                                    <!-- FIX round 9 (user, in-game: "text frame still missing, also dont see any
                                         hover effect" - round 8's geometry theory was wrong too): found the real
                                         cause by comparing against CC.ScrollHandle (OptionsVerticalScrollbarHandle
                                         below), which uses this EXACT same Brush pattern (a single BrushLayer
                                         wrapping Sprite="BlankWhiteSquare_9") and is presumed fine - the one
                                         structural difference is that it's declared as an ImageWidget, not a plain
                                         Widget. Every single documented instance of "Brush= referencing a sprite
                                         silently fails to render" in this project (this text frame, this accent
                                         bar, the old row-end diamond, the cc_flat_panel_9 redesign) was declared
                                         as a plain Widget. Strong working theory: plain Widget just doesn't draw a
                                         Brush's sprite layer at all in this engine build - only purpose-built
                                         renderable types (ImageWidget, ButtonWidget, TextWidget) do. Changed BOTH
                                         this accent bar and the text frame below from Widget to ImageWidget
                                         (Brush=/attributes otherwise unchanged) to test this directly instead of
                                         re-guessing at geometry/nesting again. -->
                                    <ImageWidget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="3" SuggestedHeight="90" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center" Brush="CC.NarrativeOptionAccent" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
                                    <!-- themed skill icon per option - see ThemeIconWidget.cs. Falls back to no
                                         sprite if ActionText doesn't match a known skill. -->
                                    <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="46" SuggestedHeight="46" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center" MarginLeft="10">
                                      <Children>
                                        <Widget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" Sprite="cc_card_9" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
                                        <ThemeIconWidget ActionText="@ActionText" WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="38" SuggestedHeight="38" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
                                      </Children>
                                    </Widget>
                                    <!-- FIX round 13 (user: two separate reports on real screenshots -
                                         "That one is conflicting" (the CC.NarrativeOptionTextFrame border
                                         doubling up on fs_tile_stone_9's own baked-in edge, see that brush's
                                         note in Brushes\CharCreation.xml) and "some texts arent fitting" (a
                                         longer ActionText - e.g. "You distinguished yourself at the defence of
                                         Osgiliath," - wraps to 2 lines and gets clipped at the old Fixed 46
                                         height, which was only ever sized for short single-line entries like
                                         "Noble Houses of Gondor"). Both fixed together: the separate border
                                         ImageWidget is gone (CC.NarrativeOptionFill puts the hover/selected
                                         brighten on the texture itself instead, see that brush), and the box
                                         height goes 46->78 (row MinHeight/accent bar 60->90 to match) - a plain
                                         fixed bump rather than true auto-height-from-text-content, since this
                                         exact row already has a documented StretchToParent-inside-CoverChildren
                                         ballooning bug risk (see the ButtonWidget's own comment above) that a
                                         dynamic CoverChildren-driven text box would likely re-trigger. 78 fits
                                         two wrapped lines of this FontSize-19 text comfortably; short
                                         single-line entries just get some extra empty space above/below, a
                                         minor look-tightness trade rather than clipped/unreadable text. If some
                                         stage's text is long enough to wrap a 3rd line, bump 78/90 further. -->
                                    <!-- FIX round 16 (user, marked-up screenshot: "Still there Look i marked it
                                         in red, that thick yellow one" - fs_tile_stone_9's own edge was STILL
                                         showing at a 14px inset; round 15's 2px bars were correctly thin but
                                         only ADDED a second border, didn't remove the first). Fill sprite
                                         swapped to ld_bar_stone (see CC.NarrativeOptionFill in
                                         Brushes\CharCreation.xml) - no baked-in edge at all, so inset shrunk
                                         back down to 2px (just enough to sit inside the hand-built border bars,
                                         no longer needs to hide anything). The 2px bars from round 15 are now
                                         the ONLY border in this construction. -->
                                    <Widget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedHeight="78" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center" MarginLeft="66" MarginRight="40" DoNotPassEventsToChildren="true">
                                      <Children>
                                        <ImageWidget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" MarginLeft="2" MarginRight="2" MarginTop="2" MarginBottom="2" Brush="CC.NarrativeOptionFill" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
                                        <Widget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedHeight="2" VerticalAlignment="Top" Sprite="BlankWhiteSquare_9" Color="#C9AB69FF" AlphaFactor="0.55" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
                                        <Widget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedHeight="2" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Sprite="BlankWhiteSquare_9" Color="#C9AB69FF" AlphaFactor="0.55" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
                                        <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" SuggestedWidth="2" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Sprite="BlankWhiteSquare_9" Color="#C9AB69FF" AlphaFactor="0.55" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
                                        <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" SuggestedWidth="2" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Sprite="BlankWhiteSquare_9" Color="#C9AB69FF" AlphaFactor="0.55" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
                                        <TextWidget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" MarginLeft="14" MarginRight="14" MarginTop="8" MarginBottom="8" VerticalAlignment="Center" Brush="CC.NarrativeOption" Text="@ActionText" />
                                      </Children>
                                    </Widget>
                                    <!-- row-end diamond ornament: static direct Sprite=/AlphaFactor= rather than a
                                         state-driven Brush= - a CC.* brush here silently failed to render for a
                                         reason not tracked down; direct Sprite= is a confirmed-working full fix. -->
                                    <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="16" SuggestedHeight="16" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Center" MarginRight="12" Sprite="fs_diamond" AlphaFactor="0.45" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
                                  </Children>
                                </ButtonWidget>
                              </ItemTemplate>
                            </NavigatableListPanel>

                            <!-- Once an option is picked: its own description + stat gain/loss summary. IsVisible
                                 lives on this OUTER wrapper (inherits the screen's own VM, where AnyItemSelected
                                 actually lives) rather than the DataSource={SelectedOption} inner child - a real
                                 scoping bug found earlier this session: once a widget's DataSource switches to a
                                 child object, ALL of that widget's own @-bindings resolve against the CHILD, and
                                 CharacterCreationOptionVM has no AnyItemSelected property, so the binding would
                                 silently resolve false and stay hidden permanently even with a real selection. -->
                            <Widget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" IsVisible="@AnyItemSelected" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" DoNotPassEventsToChildren="true">
                              <Children>
                                <Widget DataSource="{SelectedOption}" WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" MarginTop="8" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" DoNotPassEventsToChildren="true">
                                  <Children>
                                    <ListPanel WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" StackLayout.LayoutMethod="VerticalTopToBottom">
                                      <Children>
                                        <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="290" SuggestedHeight="2" Sprite="GradientDivider_9" Color="#C9AB69FF" MarginBottom="10" />
                                        <TextWidget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" MarginRight="16" MarginBottom="10" Brush="CC.NarrativeSelDesc" Text="@DescriptionText" />
                                        <RichTextWidget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" MarginRight="16" MarginBottom="6" Brush="CC.NarrativePositive" Text="@PositiveEffectText" />
                                        <RichTextWidget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="CoverChildren" MarginRight="16" Brush="CC.NarrativeNegative" Text="@NegativeEffectText" />
                                      </Children>
                                    </ListPanel>
                                  </Children>
                                </Widget>
                              </Children>
                            </Widget>

                          </Children>
                        </ListPanel>

                      </Children>
                    </Widget>

                  </Children>
                </ScrollablePanel>

                <ScrollbarWidget Id="OptionsVerticalScrollbar" WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" SuggestedWidth="4" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Center" MarginTop="10" MarginBottom="10" AlignmentAxis="Vertical" Handle="OptionsVerticalScrollbarHandle" MaxValue="100" MinValue="0">
                  <Children>
                    <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" SuggestedWidth="2" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Sprite="BlankWhiteSquare_9" AlphaFactor="0.2" Color="#C9AB69FF" />
                    <ImageWidget Id="OptionsVerticalScrollbarHandle" WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="4" SuggestedHeight="40" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Brush="CC.ScrollHandle" />
                  </Children>
                </ScrollbarWidget>

              </Children>
            </Widget>

          </Children>
        </Widget>

        <!-- TOP RIBBON: full-width strip, copied verbatim from TAOMFaceGen.xml's own ribbon (same fs_strip
             sprite/height/margins). Z-ORDER FIX (LAYOUT PASS 4): declared AFTER both panels now (was before
             them), so it draws ON TOP of them wherever they overlap - matches FaceGen's own proven ordering
             exactly (panel(s) first, ribbon after). FACTION/CHARACTER use StageJumpButton (real native
             CharacterCreationManager.GoToStage jump, see that class's own comment for the stage-index
             evidence); ORIGINS is plain static text since this screen already IS the origins/narrative
             content - no click target needed. -->
        <Widget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedHeight="90" VerticalAlignment="Top" Sprite="fs_strip" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" />
        <ListPanel WidthSizePolicy="CoverChildren" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedHeight="50" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top" MarginTop="20" StackLayout.LayoutMethod="HorizontalSpaced">
          <Children>
            <StageJumpButton DoNotPassEventsToChildren="true" StageIndex="0" WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="110" SuggestedHeight="50">
              <Children>
                <FrontEndTextWidget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" Brush="CC.TabText" LocalizedText="{=taom_fui_faction}FACTION" />
              </Children>
            </StageJumpButton>
            <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="10" SuggestedHeight="10" VerticalAlignment="Center" Sprite="fs_diamond" AlphaFactor="0.6" />
            <StageJumpButton DoNotPassEventsToChildren="true" StageIndex="1" WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="130" SuggestedHeight="50">
              <Children>
                <FrontEndTextWidget WidthSizePolicy="StretchToParent" HeightSizePolicy="StretchToParent" Brush="CC.TabText" LocalizedText="{=taom_fui_character}CHARACTER" />
              </Children>
            </StageJumpButton>
            <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="10" SuggestedHeight="10" VerticalAlignment="Center" Sprite="fs_diamond" AlphaFactor="0.6" />
            <FrontEndTextWidget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="110" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedHeight="50" Brush="CC.TabTextActive" LocalizedText="{=taom_fui_origins}ORIGINS" />
          </Children>
        </ListPanel>

        <!-- Corner ornaments ("the blending art") - LAYOUT PASS 6 (user report: "the art blending needs to be
             on the other side of the panel and flipped horizontally. Also the right screen is missing the
             blending art that the left panel has"). Both root-level siblings placed LAST so they draw on top
             of the ribbon AND both panels (FaceGen's own proven convention). Key realization: the ornament
             always decorates a panel's INNER edge - the one bordering the open viewport - not its outer edge
             against the screen boundary (confirmed by FaceGen's own RightPanel: its ornament sits on the
             panel's LEFT edge, which is the side facing the viewport, since the panel itself is on the
             right). For the ledger (now flush LEFT), its inner/viewport-facing edge is on its RIGHT, so it
             needs the FLIPPED ornament (cc_corner_ornament_l.png, a horizontally-mirrored copy made earlier
             this project) anchored from the LEFT: MarginLeft = 0 (panel's own MarginLeft) + (546-35) = 511,
             mirroring the exact "35px inside the panel's own edge" relationship the non-flipped version uses
             elsewhere. OptionsPanel (flush RIGHT) uses the ORIGINAL non-flipped ornament on ITS left/inner
             edge - the exact same formula FaceGen's own panel uses (MarginRight = 0 + (546-35) = 511) since
             both panels now share the same 546 width and flush positioning. -->
        <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="400" SuggestedHeight="300" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Top" MarginLeft="511" MarginTop="55" Sprite="cc_corner_ornament_l" AlphaFactor="0.8" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" DoNotUseCustomScaleAndChildren="true" />
        <Widget WidthSizePolicy="Fixed" HeightSizePolicy="Fixed" SuggestedWidth="400" SuggestedHeight="300" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Top" MarginRight="511" MarginTop="55" Sprite="cc_corner_ornament" AlphaFactor="0.8" DoNotAcceptEvents="true" DoNotUseCustomScaleAndChildren="true" />

        <!-- Back/Next: FIX (2026-09-26, user: "back and next button for this screen they are too big, they are
             overlapping"): copied FaceGen's own 466x64/509x70 sizing verbatim, which fit fine there since
             FaceGen has open space on the left and only ONE 546-wide panel on the right. This screen has 546-wide
             panels on BOTH sides, leaving only ~828px between them (1920-546-546) - Back(466)+Next(509)=975
             alone already exceeds that gap before any margin is even added, so they were guaranteed to overlap
             at FaceGen's size no matter how the margins were tuned. Shrunk both (same aspect ratio preserved,
             7.2727:1, so fs_confirm.png never stretches off-ratio): Back 466x64->320x44, Next 509x70->350x48.
             Margins tightened 594->586 (546+40, a slightly smaller panel-clearance gap than FaceGen's 48) -
             Back spans ~586-906, Next spans ~984-1334 on a 1920-wide screen, leaving a clean ~78px gap between
             them with no overlap. Text MarginBottom rescaled to the same ~0.14 ratio FaceGen's own buttons use. -->
        <!-- FIX round 9d (user: "still has no opacity on the background of those buttons" + "the random button
             is very small the text doesnt fit in it"): Back/Next now use CC.NarrativeConfirm (translucent
             fs_confirm, see Brushes\CharCreation.xml) instead of the fully-opaque CC.Confirm. Shrunk Back/Next
             again (260x36/290x40 -> 240x33/260x36, same 7.2727:1 aspect preserved) to open up more of the
             inter-panel gap for Random, which was far too short at 22px tall for its text to fit - rather than
             also being forced onto fs_confirm's fixed pill aspect ratio (which would demand an equally tiny
             height to stay in the gap), Random gets its OWN background: the same translucent bordered-box
             construction as the option rows' text frame (CC.NarrativeOptionTextFrame ImageWidget + a plain
             inset fill Widget) - free to size however it needs since it isn't tied to fs_confirm's shape, and
             already matches the exact "background of text with hovering... looks good" look the user just
             confirmed. RandomButton's MarginLeft is the midpoint of the ACTUAL gap between Back's right edge
             (586+240=826) and Next's left edge (1920-586-260=1074) - i.e. 950 - minus half its own width. -->
        <!-- Back/Next UNIFIED across every CC screen except Faction Select (2026-09-30) - resized 240x46/260x50
             -> 320x51/350x55, MarginBottom 46/45 -> 44/43, and MarginLeft/Right refined to 113/98 (centering
             320/350-wide buttons under each 546-wide panel - user: "should be more centered with the panels",
             see TAOMFaceGen.xml's own Back/Next comment for the full math/history). Text brush switched
             CC.ConfirmTextSmall -> CC.ConfirmText to match the now-larger shared size. Brush stays
             CC.NarrativeConfirm (translucent), not CC.Confirm - that was a deliberate, separately-requested
             look for this screen (user: "still has no opacity on the background of those buttons"), and the
             uniformity ask was about position/size, not this brush's own alpha.
             RANDOM BUTTON moved back into the bottom row, centered (same session): it briefly moved to its own
             row above Back/Next when those were still centred near the middle and left no horizontal room for
